{#- VESTA message layout — the VESTA Agent's one layout (vesta_shared/message_format.py), for the alerts Home Assistant
    sends itself, with telegram_bot.send_message parse_mode: html. Copy to /config/custom_templates/, then call the
    action homeassistant.reload_custom_templates.

    Used by INCLUDE, never import, and always "ignore missing": a missing file renders nothing and the blueprint sends
    its plain text instead — an alert never depends on this file.
        {%- set vm_title, vm_to, vm_text, vm_status = '🔥 Mains phase overload', 'Owner', 'Phase C 4450 W', '⚠️ New alert' -%}
        {% include 'vesta_message.jinja' ignore missing %}
    gives:
        <b>🔥 Mains phase overload</b>
        To: Owner
        <blockquote>Phase C 4450 W</blockquote>
        Status:
        <blockquote><i>⚠️ New alert</i></blockquote>

    "To:" follows the rule's priority when it passes one (vm_priority 'P1'…'P4': whom the VESTA Agent's alert desk
    reaches with it, its own table written below — "To: FM", "To: digest"; owner, 2026-10-19: the rules wrote that
    table by hand); else it is vm_to when a rule names who it is for; empty, it is the villa-wide
    input_text.vesta_alert_audience (one place for every alert, owner 2026-10-12). It names ROLES, as an alert card says them (message_format.audience,
    short; owner, 2026-10-16: "To: Owner", "To: FM" or "To: Owner & FM", never a name). Each role is read in any of
    its words, apart by ",": "Owner, Facility Manager" is "Owner & FM". A value naming no single role — a name, two
    joined by "&", the helper missing — is every role.

    The words themselves (roles, whom each priority reaches, stage icons and words, how a moment is written) are the
    agent's: the block between
    WORDS and END WORDS is written by vesta_shared.message_format.jinja_words — run
    `python -m vesta_shared.message_format` after changing them there; never edit it here (architecture review,
    2026-10-17: this file kept "Facility Manager" after alert cards said "FM").

    The bottom line is said by its STAGE, in the agent's own words (architecture review, 2026-10-13). A rule sets
    vm_stage — 'new', 'existing' or 'closed' — and this file writes its icon (message_format.STAGE_ICONS) before
    vm_status, or the stage's own words when there is no status (STAGE_WORDS). An all-clear gives 'closed' and no
    status: "✅ Cleared on 19/10/2026 14:05." — the agent's closing, its time this file's clock (owner, 2026-10-19:
    one closing wording; a duration the rule knows goes in its text). Without vm_stage, vm_status is written as it is
    (a rule saved before 2026-10-13). A pressed button is no longer drawn here (owner, 2026-10-19: only the agent
    chases; the task rule that drew one sent nothing since 2026-08-25).

    The tags are the agent's style table (message_format.TELEGRAM: title bold, item blockquote, note blockquote +
    italic); its test (tests/test_ha_message_layout.py) fails when this file and the agent's layout or words differ.
    Text is escaped here, once: Telegram's HTML refuses a bare "<", ">" or "&". -#}
{%- macro vm_escape(s) -%}{{ (s | default('', true) | string | trim) | replace('&', '&amp;') | replace('<', '&lt;') | replace('>', '&gt;') }}{%- endmacro -%}
{#- WORDS: written by vesta_shared.message_format.jinja_words — python -m vesta_shared.message_format -#}
{%- set vm_role_of = {"owner": "owner", "facility manager": "fm", "fm": "fm"} -%}
{%- set vm_role_words = [["owner", "Owner"], ["fm", "FM"]] -%}
{%- set vm_and = " & " -%}
{%- set vm_priority_to = {"P1": "Owner & FM", "P2": "FM", "P3": "digest", "P4": "log"} -%}
{%- set vm_icons = {"new": "⚠️", "existing": "⚠️ ⚙️", "watch": "✅", "closed": "✅"} -%}
{%- set vm_words = {"new": "New alert", "existing": "Still open", "watch": "Cleared on {time}.", "closed": "Cleared on {time}."} -%}
{%- set vm_time_format = "%d/%m/%Y %H:%M" -%}
{%- set vm_status_break = "\n" -%}
{#- END WORDS -#}
{%- set vm_by = vm_priority_to.get(vm_priority | default('', true) | string | trim | upper) -%}
{%- set vm_r = vm_to | default('', true) | string | trim -%}
{%- if not vm_r and states is defined -%}{%- set vm_r = states('input_text.vesta_alert_audience') | trim -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- set vm_named = namespace(roles=[], words=[]) -%}
{%- for vm_w in (vm_r | lower).split(',') -%}
{%- set vm_k = vm_role_of.get(vm_w | trim) -%}
{%- if vm_k -%}{%- set vm_named.roles = vm_named.roles + [vm_k] -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- for vm_k, vm_w in vm_role_words -%}
{%- if not vm_named.roles or vm_k in vm_named.roles -%}{%- set vm_named.words = vm_named.words + [vm_w] -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set vm_r = vm_by or (vm_named.words | join(vm_and)) -%}
{%- set vm_t = vm_text | default('', true) | string | trim -%}
{%- set vm_s = vm_status | default('', true) | string | trim -%}
{%- set vm_g = vm_stage | default('', true) | string | trim -%}
{%- if vm_g in vm_icons -%}
{%- set vm_at = now().strftime(vm_time_format) if now is defined else '' -%}
{%- set vm_w = vm_words.get(vm_g, '') -%}
{%- set vm_w = vm_w | replace('{time}', vm_at) if vm_at else vm_w | replace(' on {time}', '') -%}
{%- set vm_s = vm_icons[vm_g] ~ ' ' ~ (vm_s or vm_w) -%}
{%- endif -%}
<b>{{ vm_escape(vm_title) }}</b>
To: {{ vm_escape(vm_r) }}
{%- if vm_t %}
<blockquote>{{ vm_escape(vm_t) }}</blockquote>
{%- endif %}
{%- if vm_s %}{{ vm_status_break }}Status:
<blockquote><i>{{ vm_escape(vm_s) }}</i></blockquote>
{%- endif %}
